{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3TwoRow","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3TwoRow","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGaugeFixing"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.deficitA3_eq_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.deficitA3_eq_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianWordN3TwoRow.lean#L148-L175","doc":"**THE BASE-CASE PAYOFF.** The concrete `(2,1)` Brunnian-word trace, fed through the Schur–Weyl\ntwo-row reconstruction and the deficit definition, reproduces **exactly** the certified closed\nform `D_A = (−1)^{A−3} h^{2(A−1)} (h²+2)^{A−3} (h²+3)/(h²+4)` at `A = 3`:\n\n  `D₃ = h⁴ (h²+3)/(h²+4)`.\n\nThis verifies the sharpened brick-3 route (reduced Burau + two-row cap) at the base case: the\nconcrete `ρ(w₃)` — not an abstract or assumed trace — closes to the certified recursion.\n\nThe hypothesis `q² + 1 ≠ 0` is the non-degeneracy `[2] = q + q⁻¹ ≠ 0` required to normalise the\nMarkov trace by `[2]³` (it holds at the substrate anchor `q₀ ≈ 1.11` and, more generally, off the\nroots `q² = −1`); it is algebraic, not archimedean — no ordering or `Real.*` is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.hval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.hval","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianWordN3TwoRow.lean#L145-L146","doc":"`h = q − q⁻¹`, the recursion variable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.deficitA3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.deficitA3","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianWordN3TwoRow.lean#L142-L143","doc":"The convention-D deficit at `A = 3`, `D₃ = 1 − qtr(ρ(w₃))/[2]³`, built from the concrete word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.survivingQTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.survivingQTrace","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianWordN3TwoRow.lean#L136-L140","doc":"**Schur–Weyl reconstruction of the surviving quantum trace on `V^{⊗3}`** (cited, not proved):\n`qtr(ρ(w₃)) = qdim(V_{(3)})·χ^{(3)}(w₃) + qdim(V_{(2,1)})·χ^{(2,1)}(w₃) = [4]·1 + [2]·tr(w₃)`.\nOnly the two `≤2`-row partitions `(3), (2,1)` contribute (the two-row cap); `χ^{(3)}(w₃) = 1`\nbecause `w₃` is a commutator in the 1-dim symmetric channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.qBracket4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.qBracket4","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianWordN3TwoRow.lean#L133-L134","doc":"`[4] = q³ + q + q⁻¹ + q⁻³`, the `sl₂` quantum dimension of the spin-3/2 block `V_{(3)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.qBracket2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.qBracket2","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianWordN3TwoRow.lean#L130-L131","doc":"`[2] = q + q⁻¹`, the `sl₂` quantum dimension of the spin-½ block `V_{(2,1)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.brunnianW3_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.brunnianW3_trace","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianWordN3TwoRow.lean#L122-L128","doc":"**The exact `(2,1)` two-row character** `χ^{(2,1)}(w₃) = tr ρ_{(2,1)}(w₃)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.brunnianW3_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.brunnianW3_det","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianWordN3TwoRow.lean#L116-L120","doc":"**The `(2,1)` word is `SL₂`.** `det ρ_{(2,1)}(w₃) = 1` — a commutator of `det = ±1` bands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.brunnianW3_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.brunnianW3_eq","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianWordN3TwoRow.lean#L103-L114","doc":"The concrete `2×2` matrix of `ρ_{(2,1)}(w₃)`, entrywise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.brunnianW3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.brunnianW3","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianWordN3TwoRow.lean#L98-L101","doc":"**The concrete A=3 Brunnian word** `ρ_{(2,1)}(w₃)`, `w₃ = [A₀₁, A₁₂] = A₀₁ A₁₂ A₀₁⁻¹ A₁₂⁻¹`, in\nthe 2-dim reduced-Burau / `(2,1)` two-row representation of `B₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.band12Inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.band12Inv","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianWordN3TwoRow.lean#L95-L96","doc":"`A₁₂⁻¹ = σ₂⁻²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.band01Inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.band01Inv","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianWordN3TwoRow.lean#L92-L93","doc":"`A₀₁⁻¹ = σ₁⁻²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.band12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.band12","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianWordN3TwoRow.lean#L89-L90","doc":"The pure-braid band `A₁₂ = σ₂²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.band01","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.band01","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianWordN3TwoRow.lean#L86-L87","doc":"The pure-braid band `A₀₁ = σ₁²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.heckeGen2Inv_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.heckeGen2Inv_mul","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianWordN3TwoRow.lean#L79-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.heckeGen2_mul_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.heckeGen2_mul_inv","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianWordN3TwoRow.lean#L72-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.heckeGen2Inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianWordN3.heckeGen2Inv","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianWordN3TwoRow.lean#L68-L70","doc":"The inverse of `ρ(σ₂)` in the 2-dim reduced-Burau rep (`det heckeGen2 = -1`). The `σ₁` inverse\nis `QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeGen1Inv`; this supplies the missing `σ₂` one. ","signatureChunk":0}]}